    <md:content-id>m02508</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.10.7: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>1a0461b1-a262-4322-ae92-cf72dd2f2397</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="df26428d-2a6c-40d1-975e-d17e2fba4af1" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="8c25877c-9dbc-44e7-861f-f5cf0ed3b65f" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;The vertex is \\((-4, -1)\\).&quot;, &quot;The \\(x\\)-intercepts are \\((-5, 0)\\) and \\((-3, 0)\\).&quot;, &quot;The \\(y\\)-intercept is \\((0, 15)\\).&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;The \\(y\\)-intercept is \\((0, -15)\\).&quot;, &quot;The vertex is \\((-4, -1)\\).&quot;, &quot;The \\(x\\)-intercepts are \\((-5, 0)\\) and \\((-3, 0)\\).&quot;, &quot;The \\(x\\)-intercepts are \\((0, 5)\\) and \\((0, 3)\\).&quot;, &quot;The \\(x\\)-intercept is \\((0, 15)\\).&quot;, &quot;The \\(y\\)-intercept is \\((0, 15)\\).&quot;, &quot;The vertex is \\((4, -1)\\).&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>The following quadratic expressions all define the same function.</para>
      <para> \((x+5)(x+3)\) </para>
        <para> \(x^2+8x+15\) </para>
        <para> \((x+4)^2−1\) </para>
      <para><emphasis>Select three</emphasis> statements that are true about the graph of this function.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The vertex is \((-4,-1)\), the \(x\)-intercepts are \((-5,0)\) and \((-3,0)\), the \(y\)-intercept is \((0,15)\).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.1. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="d1b254ae-9370-478e-a72b-d731b6830440" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-24">
    <problem>
      <para>The following expressions all define the same quadratic function.</para>
      <para> \((x−4)(x+6)\) </para>
        <para> \(x^2+2x−24\) </para>
        <para> \((x+1)^2−25\) </para>
      <para>What is the value of the \(y\)-coordinate of the \(y\)-intercept \((0, \_\_\_)\) of the graph of the function?</para>
      <para> Enter the value of the \(y\)-coordinate.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The \(y\)-intercept is \((0,-24)\).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.1. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="bbf0723e-dd5f-4632-8aaf-6419c4973eec" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;\\((-6,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((4,0)\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((6,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((-4,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((-6,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((5,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((4,0)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> \(x\)-intercepts of the graph.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The \(x\)-intercepts of the graph are \((-6,0)\) and \((4,0)\).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.1. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="8868d88b-2575-4438-9a84-f97e79918f49" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-1">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph?</para>
      <para> Enter the \(x\)-coordinate.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph is -1.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.10.1 and 9.10.6. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2d-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e8df213e-14b1-4b54-8b38-fe140f2a3865" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-25">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph?</para>
      <para> Enter the \(y\)-coordinate.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph is -25.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.10.1 and 9.10.6. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2e-->
  <exercise data-content-id="faee25e1-e05c-447b-b41d-a7a8cb448a5f" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="Yes" data-solution-options="[&quot;Yes&quot;, &quot;No&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Is this an accurate graph of the function?</para>
      <para><figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/9aec3a655cd4d57c085d5079858841326695259b"/></media></figure></para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Yes. The \(x\)-intercepts, \(y\)-intercept, and vertex are plotted accurately.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.10.1 and 9.10.6. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="023b0c87-8a26-40f5-822f-bc7e5d89c329" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="It is half of -7 being squared." data-solution-options="[&quot;It is the substitute value for \\(x\\).&quot;, &quot;Every term in the expression was divided by 2.&quot;, &quot;It is half of -7 being squared.&quot;, &quot;Only the non-linear term was divided by 2.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Here is one way an expression in standard form is rewritten into vertex form.</para>
      <para>Original expression
        \(x^2−7x+6\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - \(x^2−7x+(-\frac{7}{2})^2+6−(-\frac{7}{2})^2\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - \((x−\frac{7}{2})^2+6−\frac{49}{4}\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - \((x−\frac{7}{2})^2+\frac{24}{4}−\frac{49}{4}\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - \((x−\frac{7}{2})^2-\frac{25}{4}\)</para>
      <para>In Step 1, where did the number \(-\frac{7}{2}\) come from?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! It is half of -7 being squared.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="f4e40af1-4c16-4820-9742-55da706419ba" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="It is added to complete the square. It is subtracted to keep the value of the expression unchanged." data-solution-options="[&quot;It is added to complete the square. It is subtracted to keep the value of the expression unchanged.&quot;, &quot;It is subtracted to complete the square. It is added to keep the value of the expression unchanged. &quot;, &quot;It is added to complete the square. It is subtracted to change the value of the expression.&quot;, &quot;It is subtracted to complete the square. It is added to change the value of the expression.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>In Step 1, why was \((-\frac{7}{2})^2\) added and then subtracted?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! It is added to complete the square. It is subtracted to keep the value of the expression unchanged.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a9cb3566-dd50-4111-9c3d-4dd33e0f0626" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="The expression, which is a perfect square, is written as a squared expression." data-solution-options="[&quot;The expression is subtracted to keep the value of the expression unchanged.&quot;, &quot;The expression, which is a perfect square, is written as a squared expression.&quot;, &quot;The expression, which is not a perfect square, is written as a squared expression.&quot;, &quot;The expression is added to keep the value of the expression unchanged.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>What happened in Step 2?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The expression, which is a perfect square, is written as a squared expression. </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3d-->
  <exercise data-content-id="953b3ef1-2fe4-4336-945a-ca2aedee3adb" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="The constant term is written as a fraction so that it has a common denominator, which makes it easier to subtract." data-solution-options="[&quot;The quadratic term is written as a fraction so that it has a common denominator, which makes it easier to subtract. &quot;, &quot;A random term was added to complete the square.&quot;, &quot;The linear term is written as a fraction so that it has a common denominator, which makes it easier to subtract.&quot;, &quot;The constant term is written as a fraction so that it has a common denominator, which makes it easier to subtract.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>What happened in Step 3?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The constant term is written as a fraction so that it has a common denominator, which makes it easier to subtract.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para> Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3e-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a043e713-3976-41a1-85a5-ba0bbb4f8b11" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="The vertex of the graph is at \((\frac{7}{2}, -6\frac{1}{4})\)." data-solution-options="[&quot;The vertex of the graph is at \\((-6\\frac{1}{4}, \\frac{7}{2})\\).&quot;, &quot;The vertex of the graph is at \\((\\frac{5}{2}, -\\frac{5}{2})\\).&quot;, &quot;The vertex of the graph is at \\((\\frac{7}{2}, -6\\frac{1}{4})\\).&quot;, &quot;The vertex of the graph is at \\((\\frac{5}{2}, -6)\\).&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>What does the last expression tell us about the vertex of the graph of a function defined by this expression?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The vertex of the graph is at \((\frac{7}{2}, -6\frac{1}{4})\).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.10.3 and 9.10.6. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="9c95eec7-1f50-47b2-b4a7-9799d8a2f05e" data-problem-comparator="text" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="+6">
    <problem>
      <para>Enter the missing number, including the sign, for the expression when \(d(x)=x^2+12x+36\) is written in vertex form.</para>
      <para>\(d(x)=(x\_\_\_)^2\).</para>
      <para> Enter the missing number, including the sign.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! +6</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--5a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="1a5fdedf-1462-4fae-bd8b-d5949c15dbcc" data-problem-comparator="text" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="+5">
    <problem>
      <para>Enter the missing numbers, including the signs, for the expression when \(f(x)=x^2+10x+21\) is written in vertex form. \(f(x)=(x + \underline{\;\mathbf a\boldsymbol.\;})^2 \underline{\;\mathbf b\boldsymbol.\;}\)</para>
      <para>What is the value of the missing number, including the sign, in the place of the letter a?
        </para>
      <para> Enter the missing number, including the sign.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! +5</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--5b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="017764f0-7d22-4926-a01a-0e8c8dfdd5a7" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-4">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the value of the missing number, including the sign, for the letter b?</para>
      <para>Enter the missing number, including the sign. </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! -4</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
